3) FULL PARTS LIST (WITH DIGI‑KEY / MOUSER EXAMPLES)
===========================================================

Core IC:
  • CD4069UBE – Hex CMOS inverter, PDIP‑14
    - Digi‑Key: 296-3518-5-ND (Texas Instruments CD4069UBE)
    - Mouser: 595-CD4069UBE (Texas Instruments CD4069UBE) 

Solar panel:
  • Small silicon calculator‑style solar cell
    - Any 2‑pin, ~1.5–3 V open‑circuit, tens of µA
    - Example: “mini solar cell 30x60 mm” (generic; pick by size)

Diode:
  • Schottky diode for low forward drop
    - Example: BAT54 series
    - Digi‑Key: BAT54CFSCT-ND or similar
    - Mouser: 771-BAT54C-7-F or similar

Capacitors:
  • C1 (reservoir): 10 µF – 47 µF, 10 V or higher
    - Type: radial electrolytic or tantalum
    - Example: 10 µF 16 V radial electrolytic
  • C2 (oscillator): 10 nF – 100 nF
    - Type: ceramic, 50 V
    - Example: 10 nF (0.01 µF) X7R

Resistors:
  • R1 (oscillator): 100 kΩ – 1 MΩ
    - 1/4 W, 5% or better
    - Example: 100 kΩ, 1/4 W, carbon film

Mechanical / electrodes:
  • Metal core rod:
    - Material: brass or stainless steel, Ø ~2–3 mm
    - Length: matches stylus body
  • Conductive rubber tip OR thin plastic cone:
    - “Capacitive stylus tip” replacement parts work well
  • Back electrode plate:
    - Thin copper or brass strip inside body, connected to GND

PCB / prototyping:
  • Single‑sided FR‑4 board, ~8–10 cm long
  • Solderless breadboard (for initial testing)
  • Hookup wire (24–26 AWG)

Enclosure:
  • Stylus‑shaped plastic tube or 3D‑printed shell
  • Adhesive or screws to mount solar panel on exterior

