Key mechanical points:

  • Metal core runs the full length, anchored at back end.
  • Tip is a rubber or thin‑plastic cap over the core.
  • Solar panel is mounted on the outer shell near the front or mid‑section.
  • Wires from solar panel go inside to the PCB.
  • PCB sits alongside or around the core.
  • Back electrode plate is glued or screwed inside the shell and wired to GND.
  • Entire outer surface (except tip and solar window) is smooth plastic.

